r_message_buffer_size and related config; test smaller values.\\n  - Check for burst amplification from batching and watermark/barrier alignment.\\n  - Collect logs around saturation events; add tracing if needed.\\n  - Propose mitigation: tuning, backoff, adaptive flush cadence, or bounded buffers.\\n\\nIssue link\\n- http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/risingwave/-/issues/19124\\n\\nOptional next refinements\\n- Add team stakeholders as watchers: provide usernames (e.g., team lead, on-call).\\n- Add any internal labels your workflow uses (e.g., SLO-breach, oncall, customer-reported).\\n- Convert the triage checklist into issue description (instead of comment), if you prefer it top-of-page.\\n\\nTell me the usernames or label names you want and I\u2019ll set them.', image_urls=None, wait_for_response=True, action='message', security_risk=None), MessageAction(content=\"Excellent job on adding those details! This will definitely help in making the issue more manageable and visible to all relevant parties.\\n\\nHere are some suggestions for further refinements:\\n\\n1. **Team Stakeholders as Watchers**: Adding specific team leads and on-call members directly as watchers can streamline communication.\\n   - **Lead**: @li.leader\\n   - **On-call**: @noel.kwan\\n\\n2. **Internal Labels**:\\n   - `SLO-breach`\\n   - `oncall`\\n   - `customer-reported`\\n\\n3. **Checklist Placement**: Since the triage checklist is vital, placing it in the issue description itself might ensure it's immediately visible and prevent it from being overlooked in the comments.\\n\\nWould you be able to add these usernames as watchers and update the internal labels? As for moving the checklist, that\u2019s your call. Keeping it in the description might be slightly more accessible. Let me know if you encounter any issues or need further adjustments!\", image_urls=None, wait_for_response=False, action='message', security_risk=None), RecallAction(recall_type='knowledge', query=\"Excellent job on a